A||||6||Carrolles||Pics of my Grooms Long Block||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||02-28-2000||11:34 PM||||Take a look.This is the Grooms long block I got through Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory.  It has an 18 month unlimited mileage warranty.  It is a stock 2.8L bored .040 over.  I port matched the intake and plenum and welded and ported the exhaust manifolds.<P>So far I am very pleased with it (about 700 miles on it now).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grooms1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grooms2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grooms3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grooms4.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||02-28-2000||11:36 PM||||The colors didn't scan very well.  Everything is newly painted the original colors.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-29-2000||05:54 AM||||Nice!  What did it cost?  How big is 40 over?  Was it sleeved or is the displacement larger?||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||02-29-2000||08:34 PM||||Either 30 or 40 overbore on a rebuilt engine is common. On a 2.8 this will increase the displacement to about 2.9 liters. Monkey, you usually don't sleeve modern cast iron blocks. When they get too thin, you throw 'em away and get another block. Those 2.8 blocks are almost literally a dime a dozen right now. Sometimes you might sleeve an aluminum block.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-29-2000||11:35 PM||||The long block was $1175 with a new oil pump and all the gaskets to complete the rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000005||b_b_a_d||03-01-2000||02:55 PM||||Beautiful photos!!!   I just love to see a new engine going together!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My wife works for US Engine over here in the Great NorthWest.  Don't think she isn't working on something special in her spare time.  LOL!||||reg||6
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-01-2000||04:45 PM||||I knew that, batboy.  I was just ummm...testing you guys. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||1
